{
  "_about": "The app's information architecture, in one file. src/ui/shell.js renders the rail and the phase bar from this and nothing else, so adding a module is a JSON edit. `status` is honest on purpose: 'built' links somewhere real, 'partial' links to the step that half-covers it today, 'planned' renders a stub that says what it will do. Never let a module claim 'built' before it is. A `global` entry may carry `modules` of its own: the Library's reference tools (case studies, dissection, the craft glossary) are tabs of library.html, not steps of a stage, so they hang off the Library rather than off a phase. Their module ids are unchanged, because plans key features by them; src/lib/navmodel.js is the one place that joins the two lists. The Blueprints are a second such shelf (feature.html, short.html): a guide that walks all five stages cannot be filed inside one of them, so each stage carries a `guide` list instead, linking to the blueprint part that covers it (`part` is the feature blueprint's Part number, one part per stage). `group` on a module is a sub-heading in its stage's menu (Pre-Production's four). `projectPages: true` on a shelf says its pages write a film, so src/ui/no-project.js gives them the no-project banner as it does a stage's pages.",
